os_linux: don't query glibc/pthread versions on android

<gnu/libc-version.h> is a glibc header with no bionic equivalent, so hotspot
does not compile for android at all:

  os_linux.cpp:98:11: fatal error: 'gnu/libc-version.h' file not found

libpthread_init() then queries _CS_GNU_LIBC_VERSION / _CS_GNU_LIBPTHREAD_VERSION
and falls back to gnu_get_libc_version(), none of which bionic has. Its pthread
implementation lives inside libc rather than a separate library, so there is no
version to report and no LinuxThreads-era flavour to detect: bionic is always
NPTL-like with floating stacks, which is what the android branch asserts
directly.

The 11+ releases carry this as patch 0002; this is the same change against 8's
older os_linux.cpp, which spells the setter set_glibc_version and has to set
the NPTL and floating-stack flags the skipped code would have set.

diff --git a/hotspot/src/os/linux/vm/os_linux.cpp b/hotspot/src/os/linux/vm/os_linux.cpp
index 09c4056..e6f719d 100644
--- a/hotspot/src/os/linux/vm/os_linux.cpp
+++ b/hotspot/src/os/linux/vm/os_linux.cpp
@@ -95,7 +95,9 @@
 # include <string.h>
 # include <syscall.h>
 # include <sys/sysinfo.h>
+#ifndef __ANDROID__
 # include <gnu/libc-version.h>
+#endif
 # include <sys/ipc.h>
 # include <sys/shm.h>
 # include <link.h>
@@ -584,6 +586,15 @@ void os::Linux::hotspot_sigmask(Thread* thread) {
 // detecting pthread library
 
 void os::Linux::libpthread_init() {
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+  // bionic defines neither _CS_GNU_LIBC_VERSION nor _CS_GNU_LIBPTHREAD_VERSION,
+  // and its pthread implementation lives inside libc rather than a separate
+  // library, so there is no version to query. It is always NPTL-like.
+  os::Linux::set_glibc_version("bionic - unknown");
+  os::Linux::set_libpthread_version("bionic - unknown");
+  os::Linux::set_is_NPTL();
+  os::Linux::set_is_floating_stack();
+#else
   // Save glibc and pthread version strings. Note that _CS_GNU_LIBC_VERSION
   // and _CS_GNU_LIBPTHREAD_VERSION are supported in glibc >= 2.3.2. Use a
   // generic name for earlier versions.
@@ -642,6 +653,7 @@ void os::Linux::libpthread_init() {
   if (os::Linux::is_NPTL() || os::Linux::supports_variable_stack_size()) {
      os::Linux::set_is_floating_stack();
   }
+#endif
 }
 
